{
  "_comment": [
    "Bundled vocabulary for the ai-inventory validator (contract requirement 3).",
    "The enums also present in contract/ai-inventory.schema.json are kept in sync by",
    "scripts/check_repo.py; if you change one, change both.",
    "",
    "What is deliberately NOT here: any framework control text or control identifier list.",
    "ISO/IEC 42001 references are free text on purpose - this repository vendors no standard's",
    "control catalogue (see contract/README.md, non-goals). The EU AI Act roles, the Article 5(1)",
    "practices, the Article 50 triggers, the Annex III areas and the four NIST AI RMF functions are",
    "named in the public instruments themselves and are enumerated here only so that a typo gets a",
    "'did you mean ...?' instead of landing in Noru.",
    "",
    "finding_categories is ordered, and the order carries meaning: prohibited practices have applied",
    "since 2 February 2025 (Article 113(a)) and transparency since 2 August 2026 (Article 113),",
    "while the obligations that follow from a risk tier apply from the later date each finding",
    "states in enforceable_from. The validator rejects a manifest whose findings block is written",
    "in another order."
  ],
